Chapter: Ieee802154EncodeTest

  cites Encode chapter Ieee802154

 Exercise IEEE 802.15.4 framing: frame-control packing, the CRC-16/
 KERMIT frame check sequence (verified against check value 0x2189 via
 the frame), and a full short-addressed data frame. Byte sequences
 checked against an independent implementation. opening returns the
 count of passing checks.

Section: Helpers

  bytes-eq : List Integer, List Integer -> Boolean
  bytes-eq (a) (b) =
   if list-length a /= list-length b then False
   else bytes-eq-loop a b 0 (list-length a)

  bytes-eq-loop : List Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  bytes-eq-loop (a) (b) (i) (len) =
   if i >= len then True
   else if list-at a i /= list-at b i then False
   else bytes-eq-loop a b (i + 1) len

  flag : Boolean -> Integer
  flag (b) = if b then 1 else 0

Section: Checks

  check-fcf : Integer
  check-fcf =
   flag (ieee-fcf ieee-type-data 0 0 0 1 ieee-addr-short 0 ieee-addr-short == #8841)

  check-fcs : Integer
  check-fcs =
   flag (ieee-fcs [65, 136, 1, 205, 171, 52, 18, 120, 86, 1, 2] == #3CBD)

  check-u16-le : Integer
  check-u16-le =
   flag (bytes-eq (ieee-u16-le #8841) [65, 136])

  check-frame : Integer
  check-frame =
   flag (bytes-eq (ieee-build-data-short 1 #ABCD #1234 #5678 [1, 2]) [65, 136, 1, 205, 171, 52, 18, 120, 86, 1, 2, 189, 60])

  opening : Integer =
   let a = check-fcf
   in let b = check-fcs
   in let c = check-u16-le
   in let d = check-frame
   in a + b + c + d
